<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1390–<a href="/years/1436">1436</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson was a Swedish mine owner from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergslagen">Bergslagen</a> mining district who led a rebellion in 1434 against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a> and his Danish bailiffs. Supported by miners, peasants and later nobles, the revolt spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and he was chosen as captain of the realm. He was murdered in 1436, but became a national hero, and his revolt began a century of conflict within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/engelbrekt-engelbrektsson.jpg" alt="Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modell_till_statyn_%C3%B6ver_Engelbrekt_Engelbrektsson_i_%C3%96rebro_(ur_Svenska_Familj-Journalen).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
